flowchart TB
accTitle: B3 broadcast receipts and verified outcome feedback
accDescr: An admitted workspace is delivered synchronously to named consumers. The service checks receipt identity and that consumed candidates are in the workspace, then records the receipt. An accepted receipt is not a useful outcome. A later verified report must reference an accepted receipt and an exact consumed candidate, pass evidence verification, and be revalidated before it can support B1 exact-revision updates or separately governed coalition feedback.
    SNAP[Admitted workspace snapshot] --> BROADCAST[Synchronous consumer calls]
    BROADCAST --> RECEIPT[Consumer receipt]
    RECEIPT --> VALIDATE{Accepted identity and candidate subset?}
    VALIDATE -->|No| REJECT[Rejected or failed receipt]
    VALIDATE -->|Yes| STORE[Persist receipt evidence]
    STORE --> REPORT[Later downstream outcome report]
    REPORT --> CHECK{Exact consumed candidate and source evidence verified?}
    CHECK -->|No| DENY[Reject outcome]
    CHECK -->|Yes| REVERIFY[Re-read and revalidate persisted evidence]
    REVERIFY --> B1[Update exact attributed B1 memory revision]
    REVERIFY --> COAL[Separate coalition feedback governance]
